{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusHookDecayBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnusHookDecayBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusHookExteriorPower","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.abs_mul_sum_esymm_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.abs_mul_sum_esymm_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusHookDecayBound.lean#L76-L84","doc":"**The sharp bound `B'_j`.** With the twist scalar `c = (4/[2]_q²)·q^{(L+2)(1−j)}` in front,\n`|c · Σ_a (e_j(μ⁺_a) − e_j(μ⁻_a))| ≤ |c| · Σ_a (e_j(|μ⁺_a|) + e_j(|μ⁻_a|))`. Composed with\n`trace_mul_curvature_eq_of_word_traces`, the left side is `|tr_hook(ρ·Ω₂^P)|` and the right side\nis the bound the probe finds strictly decreasing per dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.abs_sum_esymm_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.abs_sum_esymm_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusHookDecayBound.lean#L64-L74","doc":"**Across the commutator sum.** Each member of `Σ_a (e_j(μ⁺_a) − e_j(μ⁻_a))` is bounded by\nthe sum of the two moduli-symmetric values, so the whole signed sum is bounded by\n`Σ_a (e_j(|μ⁺_a|) + e_j(|μ⁻_a|))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.abs_esymm_le_esymm_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.abs_esymm_le_esymm_abs","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusHookDecayBound.lean#L53-L62","doc":"**Triangle inequality for the elementary symmetric sum.** `|e_j(μ)| ≤ e_j(|μ|)`: the\n`j`-th elementary symmetric function of a spectrum is bounded by the same function of its\nmoduli. This is the single inequality behind the sharp hook-column bound. ","signatureChunk":0}]}